 CODE
Art. 2.3.28. 
Joint debts 
The payment of joint debts may be pursued both against each spouse's own assets and against the joint assets.
However, the following debts may not be pursued out of the non-contracting spouse's own patrimony: 
1¡ debts contracted by one of the spouses for the needs of the household and the education of the children where they entail excessive expenses, having regard to the resources of the household; 
2¡ interest on debts belonging to one of the spouses; 
3¡ debts contracted by one of the spouses in the exercise of his or her profession; 
4¡ debts for the support of the descendants of one of the spouses.
